<Project>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>

    <!--
      TargetFramework is set PER PROJECT, the same split src/download-feedback uses and for the same
      reason:

        WaveControl        -> netstandard2.0, so `openness-cli` (net48, pinned there by
                              Siemens.Engineering) can reference it later AND a net8.0 coordinator
                              can too. A net8.0 library would be unreferenceable from the one tool
                              that eventually has to ask "is this configuration Class A?".
        WaveControl.Tests  -> net8.0; nothing in the test path is framework-sensitive.

      The library references NOTHING — no Siemens.Engineering, no Openness, no JSON package, no
      network. The classifier takes a name and a list of selection names; the marker writes a
      line-oriented text file with System.IO. That is what keeps a change here from ever triggering
      the TIA Openness (Path,FileHash) re-approval cycle a rebuild of openness-cli does, and what
      lets every test run on a machine with no TIA Portal on it.

      NOT WIRED INTO openness-cli. That is a separate, deliberate step.

      Warnings-as-errors matches the other solutions (audit F-37): there is no CI, so the compiler is
      the only thing that notices drift.
    -->
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
